WEBVTT

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.610
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.410
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.426 --> 00:00:21.151
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:28.830
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:33.170
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.050
But, with you...

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.130
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.001 --> 00:00:42.720
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:47.440
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.820
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.400
Just to survive!

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:55.360
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.200
Take this moment...

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.820
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.075
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.081 --> 00:01:04.870
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.613
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.619 --> 00:01:10.710
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.420
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.125
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.125 --> 00:01:18.292
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.292 --> 00:01:20.090
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:24.010
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:34.654 --> 00:01:39.826
We, the members of Q Class, were assigned
our first official DDS case...

00:01:40.327 --> 00:01:44.164
...to arrive in Hyoutan village and
investigate Kamikakushi village...

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:48.210
...and the truth behind the seven
disappearances in the last decade.

00:01:49.669 --> 00:01:51.838
But, the morning after we arrived...

00:01:52.464 --> 00:01:54.174
...a fellow boarder at our inn...

00:01:54.633 --> 00:01:58.762
...also a member of the TV crew sent to investigate
the treasures of the old Japanese army...

00:01:59.387 --> 00:02:01.139
...Azegami Rio-san, their reporter...

00:02:01.807 --> 00:02:05.602
...was found dead, buried in a grave.

00:02:09.856 --> 00:02:11.900
I'm Ootawara from the prefectural
police department.

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.903
Are you the owner of the inn where
the victim was staying?

00:02:15.862 --> 00:02:16.363
Yes.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.824
I would like to hear a detailed account...

00:02:19.449 --> 00:02:25.497
...of why you found it necessary to dig
up a grave to find the victim's body.

00:02:26.373 --> 00:02:27.499
Well, you see...

00:02:27.499 --> 00:02:28.875
We asked him to do it.

00:02:29.709 --> 00:02:30.919
Who are you guys?

00:02:31.753 --> 00:02:33.171
We're staying at the same inn.

00:02:34.005 --> 00:02:36.758
We deduced that her body would be in there...

00:02:37.259 --> 00:02:38.218
...and asked him to dig up the grave.

00:02:38.552 --> 00:02:40.470
That's police work!

00:02:40.971 --> 00:02:43.056
Just on the basis of some half-baked theory...

00:02:43.348 --> 00:02:45.767
...you dug up someone's grave?

00:02:45.976 --> 00:02:48.353
But, if there was no body...

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:53.984
...wouldn't the police have just written this
off as another mysterious disappearance?

00:02:54.359 --> 00:02:55.193
What?

00:02:55.652 --> 00:02:57.863
Just who the hell do you think you are...

00:02:58.196 --> 00:02:59.906
...interfering in a police investigation like this?

00:03:00.574 --> 00:03:03.827
Sir, let us explain the rest.

00:03:04.286 --> 00:03:05.120
Please do.

00:03:05.328 --> 00:03:06.872
Hey, hold on there, sir...

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.415
Now, now, detective...

00:03:09.165 --> 00:03:10.500
You brats!

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.627
I'll arrest you for interfering
with our investigation!

00:03:14.546 --> 00:03:15.922
I'm Kyuu from DDS.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.968
W-What? What did you say? DDS?

00:03:20.552 --> 00:03:21.386
I'm Amakusa.

00:03:21.678 --> 00:03:22.429
I'm Minami.

00:03:22.929 --> 00:03:23.638
I'm Touyama.

00:03:24.055 --> 00:03:24.890
I'm Narusawa.

00:03:25.724 --> 00:03:29.269
We're actually in the midst of our investigation
concerning the missing college student.

00:03:30.145 --> 00:03:31.396
Can we count on your help?

00:03:31.855 --> 00:03:34.399
Well, err... Alright...

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:35.859
Thank you very much.

00:03:36.651 --> 00:03:38.904
Then I’d like to ask you to do something.

00:03:39.988 --> 00:03:42.908
Please dig up all the graves here.

00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:45.076
A-All the graves?

00:03:45.744 --> 00:03:49.664
Within the past decade, seven people
have gone missing from this village.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.543
Are you saying that all of those
have been murder cases?

00:03:53.793 --> 00:03:56.379
I'm not saying that all of them
are necessarily like that.

00:03:57.255 --> 00:04:02.677
But, if there were others that were
killed like Azegami-san...

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:08.600
...then there is the possibility that others
may be buried here as well.

00:04:09.225 --> 00:04:10.644
A-Alright...

00:04:17.317 --> 00:04:20.111
Our DDS notebooks are really amazing.

00:04:20.862 --> 00:04:25.450
It really conveys the authority of the
master detective, Dan Morihiko.

00:04:26.409 --> 00:04:28.453
But your problems start here.

00:04:29.079 --> 00:04:33.750
There's no doubt about this picture that the
reporter Azegami Rio-san was holding.

00:04:34.459 --> 00:04:37.504
Especially since there is evidence that the
perpetrator attempted to forcibly take it.

00:04:38.004 --> 00:04:41.758
This is definitely the reason why she was killed.

00:04:43.593 --> 00:04:46.972
It looks like the numerical infinity sign.

00:04:47.597 --> 00:04:49.557
It also looks like a Moebius strip.

00:04:50.058 --> 00:04:53.311
You guys are trying too hard.
It's the number eight!

00:04:53.645 --> 00:04:55.146
It's just turned sideways.

00:04:56.272 --> 00:04:57.482
That's not right.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:02.278
This is a secret code connected to the
treasures of the old Japanese army.

00:05:02.696 --> 00:05:03.613
Those who break the code...

00:05:03.613 --> 00:05:07.117
...and discover the location of the treasure
trove, are being killed one after another.

00:05:07.617 --> 00:05:10.078
Would that not be a motive
for murdering people?

00:05:10.829 --> 00:05:14.833
Anyway, with this murder case was here in Hyoutan village...

00:05:15.625 --> 00:05:17.836
...there's a reason for Kyuu and you guys to stay.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.631
Megu and I will go to Kamikakushi village.

00:05:22.507 --> 00:05:23.717
But be careful.

00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:28.471
Remember what the inn owner's son, Ryan, said.

00:05:29.431 --> 00:05:31.182
"This is only the beginning."

00:05:31.683 --> 00:05:32.809
You mean the message from the high priest?

00:05:33.309 --> 00:05:33.935
Yeah.

00:05:34.227 --> 00:05:39.232
It sounds as if the high priest knows
that things will happen.

00:05:40.442 --> 00:05:41.526
Now that you mention it...

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.279
Ryu, we're going too.

00:05:44.946 --> 00:05:45.989
But what about the masks?

00:05:46.823 --> 00:05:49.492
You can't get into Kamikakushi
village without a mask.

00:05:50.577 --> 00:05:53.288
There's a checkpoint right by the exit.

00:05:53.997 --> 00:05:54.831
We'll go that far.

00:05:55.665 --> 00:05:59.586
I'm worried about you two,
and I want to see it too...

00:06:01.046 --> 00:06:02.130
That Kamikakushi village.

00:06:03.882 --> 00:06:07.260
This is the tunnel connecting
to Kamikakushi village.

00:06:08.094 --> 00:06:08.720
Wow!

00:06:09.054 --> 00:06:13.308
This tunnel is even narrower and darker than the
one we went through to get to Hyoutan village.

00:06:13.808 --> 00:06:16.895
You don't need to wear the mask in the tunnel.

00:06:17.062 --> 00:06:19.397
But on the other side is an Ekishin village.

00:06:20.148 --> 00:06:24.652
Please keep in mind that only those with masks
may proceed beyond the checkpoint.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:25.945
Thanks.

00:06:26.529 --> 00:06:28.198
Megu, you have your mask?

00:06:29.574 --> 00:06:30.825
Alright, then let's go.

00:06:33.369 --> 00:06:34.746
Okay, let's go too.

00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:41.795
I wonder how much longer we have to walk...

00:06:42.545 --> 00:06:44.506
It's said to be 1.5 kilometers long.

00:06:45.006 --> 00:06:50.345
With the stairs in the middle, it's supposed
to take 30 minutes each way.

00:06:50.887 --> 00:06:52.847
We're going to be in here for 30 minutes?

00:06:53.348 --> 00:06:56.434
Aside from this tunnel, it appears
that there really is no other route.

00:06:56.434 --> 00:06:56.559
Aside from this tunnel, it appears
that there really is no er route.

00:06:56.559 --> 00:06:58.269
Aside from this tunnel, it appears
that there really is no other route.

00:06:59.312 --> 00:07:02.273
Look, those are the electric and phone lines.

00:07:03.274 --> 00:07:06.820
In the mountains, they generally use
the shortest path with steel towers.

00:07:07.153 --> 00:07:09.197
But here they're using this tunnel instead.

00:07:09.948 --> 00:07:13.201
It's almost like the tunnel to the
Kurobe Dam at Mt. Tateyama.

00:07:13.618 --> 00:07:15.453
So that's what "solitary island of flat land" means....

00:07:18.164 --> 00:07:18.790
There's the stairs.

00:07:19.874 --> 00:07:20.792
It's a spiral staircase.

00:07:21.417 --> 00:07:23.795
Kazuma, how long have we been walking?

00:07:25.463 --> 00:07:26.297
About 15 minutes.

00:07:26.673 --> 00:07:31.261
So that means we're exactly halfway
through this 30 minute tunnel.

00:07:49.654 --> 00:07:51.239
Hey, hold it...

00:07:52.323 --> 00:07:54.200
Don't walk so fast...

00:07:54.701 --> 00:07:55.994
Geez, you're pitiful.

00:07:56.578 --> 00:07:59.914
You just can't keep up because you always
sit in front of your computer.

00:08:01.958 --> 00:08:02.625
What's wrong?

00:08:03.626 --> 00:08:06.004
I'm hearing footsteps closing in on us.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:16.181
What? Maybe the killer is coming for us?

00:08:16.681 --> 00:08:18.766
Don't say stuff like that.

00:08:19.475 --> 00:08:20.018
Let's hurry.

00:08:23.271 --> 00:08:26.691
Wait, don't leave me behind!

00:08:37.368 --> 00:08:37.785
Kazuma!

00:08:38.203 --> 00:08:38.870
Are you alright?

00:08:41.206 --> 00:08:44.250
Ah, it's the kids from the detective club.

00:08:45.627 --> 00:08:46.628
The TV crew...

00:08:46.836 --> 00:08:49.088
Don't scare us like that.

00:08:49.255 --> 00:08:51.049
Who's scaring who here?

00:08:51.633 --> 00:08:53.801
You guys are going to Kamikakushi village too?

00:08:54.385 --> 00:08:55.720
Y-yeah.

00:08:56.137 --> 00:08:59.098
I don't know if you're a detective
club or whatever, but let it be.

00:08:59.557 --> 00:09:02.810
If you get into this, thinking it's some
sort of game, you'll get hurt.

00:09:03.436 --> 00:09:04.771
What about you TV guys?

00:09:05.188 --> 00:09:08.524
You just had one of your crew murdered and are
still thinking about continuing your shoot?

00:09:08.942 --> 00:09:11.694
What are you trying to say you little runt?

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.072
I'll put you in your place if
you keep talking like that!

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.990
Iwashimizu-san, cut it out.

00:09:16.199 --> 00:09:17.909
These kids aren't worth the trouble.

00:09:18.409 --> 00:09:19.702
The more the merrier.

00:09:20.036 --> 00:09:22.330
How about we go together?

00:09:23.164 --> 00:09:25.750
It also feels safer if there's more people, right?

00:09:26.376 --> 00:09:27.043
It does, doesn't it?

00:09:27.961 --> 00:09:29.420
Okay, whatever.

00:09:41.015 --> 00:09:43.309
Ah, I can finally see the exit.

00:09:43.893 --> 00:09:45.603
Oowada-chan, get the camera ready please.

00:09:46.229 --> 00:09:48.231
We'll get a shot of the checkpoint,
just for good measure.

00:09:48.898 --> 00:09:51.693
You're really continuing this treasure hunt?

00:09:52.068 --> 00:09:54.279
Now that something like that
happened to Azegami...

00:09:55.071 --> 00:09:57.865
...someone will have to take responsibility
for it if we don't find something.

00:09:58.241 --> 00:09:59.367
That's the deal.

00:09:59.867 --> 00:10:03.997
We find the treasure, get the
scoop, and we get rich.

00:10:04.372 --> 00:10:06.958
If we mess up we might all get fired.

00:10:07.375 --> 00:10:11.587
And I'm kind of getting warmed up here.

00:10:11.629 --> 00:10:13.589
Warmed up, why's that?

00:10:15.633 --> 00:10:17.051
Because of this, this here.

00:10:19.554 --> 00:10:24.225
I think I kind of know the meaning of the
picture Azegami-Chan was holding.

00:10:26.227 --> 00:10:26.978
He figured it out?

00:10:27.854 --> 00:10:28.938
The meaning of that picture?

00:10:29.522 --> 00:10:34.277
I'm thinking about going on a little excursion
once we get to Kamikakushi village.

00:10:34.652 --> 00:10:37.530
Oowada-Chan, I'll borrow your camcorder then.

00:10:38.656 --> 00:10:39.907
Then why don't I just go with you?

00:10:40.325 --> 00:10:42.327
Hey, bring me along as well!

00:10:42.744 --> 00:10:44.078
I can’t do that!

00:10:45.413 --> 00:10:48.916
My cut will be smaller if there are more
people when I discover the treasure!

00:11:11.265 --> 00:11:12.558
Get away from the high priest!

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:14.351
I'm sorry, high priest sir.

00:11:15.269 --> 00:11:17.438
This person is actually a legitimate guest.

00:11:18.022 --> 00:11:19.440
He even has a mask.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:25.696
Everyone, this is where Kamikakushi
village begins.

00:11:26.488 --> 00:11:27.072
That's...

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.742
...the Ekishin high priest...

00:11:31.035 --> 00:11:35.414
Those from the detective club without
masks will have to turn back now.

00:11:35.789 --> 00:11:37.207
Yes, we know.

00:11:37.875 --> 00:11:39.293
Well, we're off then.

00:11:39.919 --> 00:11:40.419
Yeah.

00:11:41.128 --> 00:11:43.756
Well then, please put on your masks.

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:51.680
He disappeared...

00:11:52.389 --> 00:11:53.933
Everyone, please follow me.

00:12:03.651 --> 00:12:07.071
This is the branch house of the Ryouzanpaku Inn.

00:12:17.039 --> 00:12:20.376
Excuse me, Kurozumi-san,
what's that over there?

00:12:21.126 --> 00:12:25.255
That's the head Ekishin temple, consecrated
to our god, Ekigami-sama.

00:12:27.174 --> 00:12:30.260
The high priest lives beyond that wall.

00:12:31.303 --> 00:12:36.308
No one but the high priest is
allowed beyond those gates.

00:12:37.393 --> 00:12:41.438
Please try to stay away from it.

00:12:43.816 --> 00:12:46.443
I couldn't have used a modular cable here.

00:12:46.568 --> 00:12:48.612
Good thing I brought a coupler along.

00:12:49.321 --> 00:12:52.116
Kazuma, what the heck are you doing?

00:12:52.491 --> 00:12:55.411
I'm connecting to the missing
college students circle...

00:12:55.619 --> 00:12:57.287
...and gathering some information.

00:12:57.579 --> 00:13:02.543
The reason you're out of breath after a few measly
stairs is because all you do is stuff like that.

00:13:02.876 --> 00:13:04.169
I don't need you to lecture me.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:06.463
Alright, I got access.

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.049
Hey, Kinta...

00:13:09.883 --> 00:13:11.719
...there's something that bugs me.

00:13:13.512 --> 00:13:14.013
What's that?

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:16.682
Well, usually towns and villages
are built around places...

00:13:17.474 --> 00:13:21.687
...that have some conditions that make
it easier to live there, right?

00:13:22.521 --> 00:13:23.397
That's right.

00:13:24.064 --> 00:13:28.527
Even cities in the middle of the
desert are built by an oasis.

00:13:28.694 --> 00:13:31.989
Hyoutan village and Kamikakushi village...

00:13:32.448 --> 00:13:34.491
Why were these villages built?

00:13:34.992 --> 00:13:35.367
Huh?

00:13:36.326 --> 00:13:38.662
Well, from the bus stop...

00:13:39.121 --> 00:13:42.875
...you need to traverse a long
tunnel just to get here, right?

00:13:43.959 --> 00:13:46.086
To top it off, you have to walk
another 30 minutes...

00:13:46.503 --> 00:13:49.089
...through a tunnel to get to Kamikakushi village.

00:13:50.215 --> 00:13:54.303
I wonder when and why these
two hard-to-reach and...

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:56.930
...unimportant villages were built.

00:13:57.556 --> 00:13:58.599
I see.

00:13:59.141 --> 00:14:02.352
What sort of benefits come from here...

00:14:02.811 --> 00:14:05.230
It's perfect for hiding a treasure, isn't it?

00:14:06.315 --> 00:14:07.107
Or, alternatively...

00:14:07.733 --> 00:14:13.405
...something shady that nobody should
know about was done here.

00:14:14.073 --> 00:14:15.157
Something shady...

00:14:16.158 --> 00:14:18.494
Alright, sitting around like this does nothing.

00:14:19.369 --> 00:14:21.371
Let's walk around the village
and see if we find something.

00:14:22.039 --> 00:14:22.706
Alright!

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.044
After all, you gotta do some real
footwork to get information.

00:14:27.544 --> 00:14:28.879
Kazuma, let's go.

00:14:29.671 --> 00:14:31.715
Didn't I tell you that I don't want to go?

00:14:32.049 --> 00:14:32.716
Oh, I see...

00:14:36.512 --> 00:14:39.807
So this is the room the missing
college student stayed in.

00:14:40.682 --> 00:14:42.059
Look, Ryu-kun.

00:14:43.185 --> 00:14:44.645
This is identical to the diorama we saw.

00:14:45.813 --> 00:14:46.271
Yeah.

00:14:47.189 --> 00:14:51.568
So as theorized, the perpetrator used the
rubber raft to make those footprints.

00:14:52.027 --> 00:14:52.694
If that's the case...

00:14:53.403 --> 00:14:56.573
...that also means that the college
student is no longer alive.

00:14:57.658 --> 00:15:00.786
Just like the reporter that was buried
in the Hyoutan village's graveyard.

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:05.541
That's...

00:15:06.959 --> 00:15:08.752
The director, Anzai-san.

00:15:09.586 --> 00:15:13.799
He said that he'd solved the mystery
behind the infinity sign.

00:15:14.299 --> 00:15:15.175
I wonder if that's true.

00:15:15.634 --> 00:15:16.218
Who knows...

00:15:17.261 --> 00:15:18.720
The only thing that's certain...

00:15:19.388 --> 00:15:22.891
...is that two people have disappeared
because of the drawing.

00:15:24.268 --> 00:15:26.687
He should be careful as well.

00:15:30.065 --> 00:15:31.400
Megu, is something wrong?

00:15:32.192 --> 00:15:36.196
No, it's just that you kind of...

00:15:36.989 --> 00:15:40.200
...looked like you were waiting
for something to happen.

00:15:42.202 --> 00:15:44.204
I'm sorry. I'm saying weird things.

00:15:45.247 --> 00:15:47.416
No, you might be right...

00:15:47.833 --> 00:15:48.375
What?

00:15:49.001 --> 00:15:52.629
Even in the middle of this case...

00:15:53.714 --> 00:15:55.757
...I'm intensely drawn towards something.

00:15:56.633 --> 00:15:57.384
Something?

00:15:58.177 --> 00:16:01.013
They keep becoming more and more intense...

00:16:02.514 --> 00:16:03.182
...the mysteries.

00:16:07.102 --> 00:16:11.815
There's nothing that resembles
a clue in this village.

00:16:12.524 --> 00:16:15.152
No, there's something weird about this village.

00:16:15.819 --> 00:16:16.361
What is?

00:16:17.112 --> 00:16:18.363
Look, that hospital.

00:16:19.823 --> 00:16:21.617
Even though we're in the middle of mountains...

00:16:21.867 --> 00:16:24.036
...that building is made of concrete
and is rather luxurious.

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:28.248
Now that you mention it, it seems a little
out of proportion here for this village.

00:16:28.832 --> 00:16:31.710
And the cliffs surrounding this place...

00:16:32.669 --> 00:16:36.632
...many places look as if they were
made steeper on purpose.

00:16:37.216 --> 00:16:40.219
Just like some sort of prison that once
you're in, you can't get out of.

00:16:42.095 --> 00:16:46.350
And this dam is kind of over the top too.

00:16:53.732 --> 00:16:56.401
Geez, where have you two been?

00:16:56.985 --> 00:16:57.778
What's up?

00:16:58.403 --> 00:16:59.404
Did you find something out?

00:16:59.947 --> 00:17:01.823
That's an understatement if I ever heard one!

00:17:02.199 --> 00:17:03.742
I found something amazing.

00:17:06.078 --> 00:17:06.828
Take a look at this!

00:17:07.287 --> 00:17:08.789
What the heck is that?

00:17:09.498 --> 00:17:12.251
It's part of some highly classified documents
by the old Japanese army...

00:17:12.626 --> 00:17:14.711
...concerning these two villages.

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:18.799
This is probably a cipher where
each letter is a number.

00:17:19.466 --> 00:17:20.175
Cipher?

00:17:21.218 --> 00:17:22.594
Kazuma, can you decipher something like this?

00:17:23.011 --> 00:17:25.639
There's always a certain rule to every cipher.

00:17:26.139 --> 00:17:27.724
Once you find out what that rule is...

00:17:28.058 --> 00:17:28.976
...you should be able to decipher it.

00:17:29.518 --> 00:17:29.935
Rule?

00:17:30.269 --> 00:17:32.104
The trick to breaking ciphers like this:

00:17:32.396 --> 00:17:35.649
You take a look at common numbers...

00:17:35.941 --> 00:17:37.859
...and try to figure out their meaning.

00:17:38.277 --> 00:17:39.820
Ah it's no good.

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:41.488
I'm lousy at stuff like this...

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:42.531
For instance...

00:17:43.156 --> 00:17:49.162
Sequences like 35, 1, 33, 28, 9, (28), 48 or...

00:17:49.496 --> 00:17:54.251
...5, 24, 18 and 24 occur very often, right?

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:55.419
You're right!

00:17:55.919 --> 00:17:59.881
Anyway, I'll look for the pattern
and decipher this text.

00:18:00.257 --> 00:18:01.842
Wow, I knew that you're good at stuff like this!

00:18:02.092 --> 00:18:03.427
If you decipher this text...

00:18:03.719 --> 00:18:05.846
...we might make a big step
towards solving this case!

00:18:06.471 --> 00:18:09.474
Sometimes even you can be of some use!

00:18:10.809 --> 00:18:12.311
Why did you hit me?

00:18:14.062 --> 00:18:15.731
Did you find Anzai?

00:18:16.189 --> 00:18:17.566
No, I couldn't find him anywhere...

00:18:17.899 --> 00:18:18.775
Iwashimizu-san!

00:18:19.776 --> 00:18:21.194
My camcorder is gone!

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:22.321
What?

00:18:22.904 --> 00:18:27.367
That bastard really went out alone
looking for the treasure.

00:18:27.701 --> 00:18:28.535
Iwashimizu-san...

00:18:29.953 --> 00:18:34.666
Actually, this was just delivered to our doorstep.

00:18:35.751 --> 00:18:38.295
Oowada! This is your camcorder isn't it?

00:18:38.712 --> 00:18:40.672
Y-Yeah! That's mine.

00:18:41.548 --> 00:18:43.425
If you're looking for Anzai-san, we...

00:18:43.592 --> 00:18:44.134
Kurozumi-san...

00:18:44.926 --> 00:18:46.803
...who brought that here?

00:18:47.512 --> 00:18:49.181
I guess someone from the village.

00:18:50.432 --> 00:18:52.851
The TV station's logo is on the camera.

00:18:53.769 --> 00:18:57.522
And the whole village knows you're staying here.

00:18:58.398 --> 00:19:01.693
So you didn't see who brought the camera here...

00:19:06.948 --> 00:19:08.325
The tape's still in here.

00:19:09.076 --> 00:19:10.744
Is the tape watchable?

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:13.872
The camera's broken so I'm
not sure if we can replay...

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:15.540
Oh, it works!

00:19:15.874 --> 00:19:19.169
Hello, this is Anzai, the director.

00:19:19.711 --> 00:19:22.714
I will be following a hint I got from a villager...

00:19:22.881 --> 00:19:26.885
...heading to where the treasure of the
old Japanese army may be hidden.

00:19:27.302 --> 00:19:29.679
That idiot, does he think he's a reporter or what?

00:19:29.805 --> 00:19:33.725
Now, after a little walk I should
get to a small shrine.

00:19:34.351 --> 00:19:35.018
Small shrine?

00:19:35.602 --> 00:19:40.524
I was told that this shrine belongs to the Ekishin
religion that rules this Kamikakushi village.

00:19:40.899 --> 00:19:42.442
As the shrine is guarded by the followers...

00:19:42.609 --> 00:19:43.485
...you can't get close during the day.

00:19:43.652 --> 00:19:48.323
That's why I'm on my way there at
night, after the guards are gone.

00:19:49.032 --> 00:19:50.575
Since it looks like it's a ways off...

00:19:51.076 --> 00:19:53.912
...I'll turn off the camera to save battery.

00:19:54.329 --> 00:19:54.830
Bye!

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:56.873
Ah, that bastard turned it off!

00:19:57.416 --> 00:19:59.960
I've never heard of such a shrine.

00:20:01.211 --> 00:20:02.129
Really?

00:20:04.005 --> 00:20:04.798
The camera is back on.

00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:08.051
You can't tell where he is from this picture.

00:20:08.301 --> 00:20:10.178
It looks like he is moving towards the rice fields.

00:20:10.887 --> 00:20:14.891
I'll be moving on a footpath now,
so the camera will shake a bit.

00:20:20.063 --> 00:20:23.275
Hm? There's an obstacle here...

00:20:23.692 --> 00:20:24.651
I'll just...

00:20:26.194 --> 00:20:26.736
What's going on?

00:20:34.536 --> 00:20:35.162
The screen's...

00:20:36.455 --> 00:20:37.622
...going higher and higher...

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:47.549
This can't be...

00:20:47.757 --> 00:20:48.467
...he was abducted...

00:20:48.467 --> 00:20:49.384
...into the sky...

00:20:50.135 --> 00:20:51.386
A mysterious disappearance...

00:20:52.345 --> 00:20:53.555
He was "spirited away"!

00:20:54.556 --> 00:20:55.849
That was the anger of Ekigami-sama!

00:21:16.119 --> 00:21:18.872
In the end I couldn't get much sleep.

00:21:20.665 --> 00:21:22.417
I mean even though I barricaded
the door like that...

00:21:23.001 --> 00:21:27.005
...if the murderer really wanted to come
in, it wouldn't have lasted long.

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:31.009
Who is it?

00:21:31.885 --> 00:21:32.928
Good morning, it's me.

00:21:34.012 --> 00:21:34.638
Ryu-kun.

00:21:35.263 --> 00:21:36.556
Megu, can you do me a favor?

00:21:37.224 --> 00:21:39.184
Er, hold on a sec.

00:21:41.937 --> 00:21:43.355
Sorry for waking you up.

00:21:43.897 --> 00:21:46.191
No problem, so, what's up?
1

00:21:46.816 --> 00:21:49.569
I've got last night's video in here.

00:21:50.987 --> 00:21:56.201
Last night I had the camera guy, Oowada-san,
copy the tape onto my camcorder.

00:21:57.827 --> 00:21:58.578
I see...

00:21:59.371 --> 00:22:02.332
Using your photographic memory and this tape...

00:22:03.083 --> 00:22:05.293
...I want to determine the location
where Anzai-san disappeared.

00:22:06.044 --> 00:22:06.795
The location?

00:22:07.379 --> 00:22:08.463
Will you help me?

00:22:09.381 --> 00:22:10.924
Yeah, alright.

00:22:20.183 --> 00:22:20.600
Pause it.

00:22:21.851 --> 00:22:22.519
This tree...

00:22:26.565 --> 00:22:27.232
It's the one over there!

00:22:27.691 --> 00:22:29.568
Great, Megu. Keep it up.

00:22:30.193 --> 00:22:30.569
Yeah.

00:22:36.950 --> 00:22:39.744
The video is at night so you
can't really see much...

00:22:40.328 --> 00:22:44.541
...but, perhaps there's a tall tree in the area
that could be used to hang a person from.

00:22:45.125 --> 00:22:47.043
Yeah, maybe.

00:22:52.799 --> 00:22:53.425
This is it.

00:22:54.175 --> 00:22:55.093
See? Over there!

00:22:55.802 --> 00:23:00.765
Anzai-san was abducted into the
air over by those little twigs.

00:23:03.268 --> 00:23:04.936
But, this place...

00:23:07.856 --> 00:23:12.110
There isn't anything around that could
be used to hang someone from.

00:23:14.321 --> 00:23:14.779
I see!

00:23:15.363 --> 00:23:15.780
What?

00:23:16.323 --> 00:23:17.032
I got it!

00:23:18.116 --> 00:23:19.701
This wasn't a mysterious disappearance.

00:23:20.619 --> 00:23:23.455
This was a horrible trap to lure Director
Anzai with hints about the treasure...

00:23:24.122 --> 00:23:28.209
...and kill him in an instant
by hurling him into the air.

00:23:30.962 --> 00:23:33.006
This was a trick to disguise a murder
as a mysterious disappearance!

00:23:37.250 --> 00:23:40.503
The Sun is setting in a red glow...

00:23:41.088 --> 00:23:43.597
...as it follows me.

00:23:43.955 --> 00:23:46.780
Along this deserted beach...

00:23:46.772 --> 00:23:50.693
...I walk alone once more.

00:23:50.706 --> 00:23:54.075
I can't continue to hold in...

00:23:54.737 --> 00:23:57.090
...the tears that should pour out.

00:23:57.738 --> 00:24:00.167
Why have these memories...

00:24:00.169 --> 00:24:03.699
...become so wonderful?

00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:09.266
Ah... Like an ocean wave, I return to you...

00:24:09.516 --> 00:24:12.039
...because I'm so in love.

00:24:12.770 --> 00:24:15.756
And, now my heart...

00:24:15.761 --> 00:24:17.900
...is heavy with pain.

00:24:18.877 --> 00:24:21.794
Reflections of a bright rainbow...

00:24:21.897 --> 00:24:26.057
...shine on the distant shores of yesterday.

00:24:26.397 --> 00:24:30.028
I'll never forget those days...

00:24:30.035 --> 00:24:35.103
...and I long to see you again.

00:24:37.563 --> 00:24:39.607
Ryu proves that these mysterious
disappearances...

00:24:39.899 --> 00:24:42.610
...are actually crimes committed by someone.

00:24:43.194 --> 00:24:45.196
Megu and Ryu are confronted by the high priest.

00:24:45.780 --> 00:24:50.201
While researching the myth about the treasure,
Kazuma discovers the ugly truth of this village.

00:24:50.743 --> 00:24:52.870
And then the third "mysterious
disappearance" happens.

00:24:53.621 --> 00:24:54.664
There's only one answer!

00:24:58.042 --> 00:24:59.126
It's me, Nanami.

00:24:59.418 --> 00:25:02.588
So, did you figure out where
I was hiding this week?

00:25:03.005 --> 00:25:03.965
The answer is...
